<title>BELGIUM: Vermeulen/BBL rates Solvay &quot;sell&quot;.</title>
<headline>Vermeulen/BBL rates Solvay &quot;sell&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report -</p>
<p>    Co name----------Sector-----Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>    Solvay	   Chemicals   20,750 * Vermeulen Raemdonck/BBL</p>
<p>COMMENT ON 1996 RESULTS: In the Alkalis sector caustic soda prices have slumped since mid 1996 and no improvement in sight, but no further crash expected. In plastics, prices continue to recover and volumes are growing but raw material costs (ethylene) are also edging up. Our data (plastics and ethylene prices) clearly show weaker margins. Dividend unchanged at BFR 550 (we expected 575) is a little disappointing. EPS and rating forecasts remain unchanged.</p>
<p>Recommendation: SELL.</p>
<p>(*) Date of research report: 01/04/97/</p>
<p>    Estimates:   EPS	   pvs est  P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1997	   1,430 BFR   n/a	14.5    575 BFR</p>
<p>    1998	   1,278 BFR   n/a	16.2    575 BFR</p>
